; X-Ways drives behaviour off this export table: an exported no-op still gets
; called (export BOTH per-item callbacks and both fire per item - the "2N"
; trap). To turn a callback off, comment its line out here with ';' rather
; than stubbing it. See docs/xtension-invocation.md.
LIBRARY my_xtension
EXPORTS
    XT_Init
    XT_About
    XT_Prepare
    XT_ProcessItem
;   XT_ProcessItemEx     ; stub in the .cpp — the wrapper collects IDs in
;                        ; XT_ProcessItem. Uncomment only if you need hItem
;                        ; per item, then dedup — both fire when both exported.
;   XT_ProcessSearchHit  ; stub — uncomment when you implement search hits.
    XT_Finalize
    XT_Done
